  "details": "<p>The Assyrian king Sargon II (r. 721-705 BC) states in several of his inscriptions that he fortified Uargin, Usi, and Usian against Musku (Phrygia). All three are generally assumed to have been located in the vicinity of <a href=\"../628982\"><span>Til-garimmu</span></a>, a fortified city in <a href=\"../319432673\"><span>Kammanu/Meliddu</span></a>, on the border of <a href=\"../129678075\"><span>Tab\u0101lu</span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>E. Forrer suggested that Usian<span class=\"highlightedSearchTerm\"></span>\u00a0should be identified as classical <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/619117\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Osiena</a>\u00a0(possibly G\u00f6stesin), which is ca. 38 km northeast of Aksaray (classical\u00a0<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../619164\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Garsaura</a>).\u00a0Forrer's speculative proposal is not entirely convincing since that suggested location is rather far from Til-garimmu, assuming that Usian\u00a0was actually in close proximity to it, as Sargon's inscriptions seem to indicate.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A fortress in the vicinity of Til-garimmu fortified by the Assyrian king Sargon II (r. 721-705 BC) against Musku (Phrygia).",
